title The page that became its own ancestor
prompt the baton, unattended -- lap 3959
rota lap 3959, row 4 -- Earth by the modulus, and Earth had already been read twice today (20260905.083758 and 20260905.090338), so the row advanced by hand to Air, unread this day: law and boundary, whose sense is touch and whose dual seat is Gauge Style, this lane's own instrument.
think My two standing rows both wait on Keaton (%430 edits a seated assertion, %431 touches gate %1), so the lane's agent-doable queue was empty at the open and the lap had to find its own work. The rota found it, which is the argument for the rota.
think Air reads by running a hand along edges, and its fixed seat is foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md, whose own test is that you check whether a part stands free by trying to pull it out. I pulled on its first line and it came away in my hand: the header says a Gauge reimagining of [20260823-204456_single-stranded.md], which stays whole as the fossil -- a link to the page the reader is already standing on.
think Two claims are false in one sentence, and I checked both rather than one. The link opens the current page rather than the elder; and the elder it means, 20260618-182412_single-stranded.md, is not in the tree at all -- git log --diff-filter=D found it deleted in f758efdb2 on 20260826, one of eleven foundation fossils shed in a single commit on Keaton's circled Class M word. The shed was correct; what nobody swept was the mutants' own headers.
think The census before the diagnosis. Over 5,455 tracked markdown files, 35 carry a link to their own basename. Nine are living foundations, one is in expanding-prompts/yonder, and 25 are session logs -- testimony that keeps every word it wrote. Of the nine, SEVEN are Kin lines listing sibling pages (the four voices, the three module pages), where naming the page you stand on is ordinary and the sentence is true. Only two sit on a provenance line, and they are the two I found.
think That split is the whole design of the guard, and it came from measurement rather than from taste. A blanket self-link check would red seven honest pages on its first run and be turned off inside a week.
think The root is sharper than a stale header. At birth on c476741aa the line named the elder correctly. It was rewritten on 0877e2b5a -- the commit whose own body records eleven foundations re-seating and the lost-reference census going 178 to 390, then 347 after repointing every living citer, then 168 after the exclusions, with LOST_CEILING falling 178 to 168. My two lines were rewritten inside that repair, and by leaving a resolving link they were counted as part of it.
think I nearly blamed the wrong instrument. dated_path_repoint.rish looked like the culprit until I read its header and its scan at line 95: living files only -- a dated basename is testimony and is never opened for writing here. Both foundations carry a stamped basename, so the tool refuses them by rule. No tool did this; a hand repointed by name.
think That refusal is itself the second finding. A foundation carries a one-clock stamp in its basename AND declares Status Living, so the tree's own testimony test and the foundations' own headers disagree about what these files are. The sweep no tool would perform was performed by hand, with nothing checking it afterward.
obs Then the question that turns two bad headers into a red worth a loom: why did nothing catch it in ten days. Because a self-link RESOLVES. tracked_link_scan.sh keeps a candidate only where [ -e "$resolved" ], living_docs_lint's broken-link duty tests the same way, and qa_report_card.sh scores Truth by counting cited paths that FAIL to resolve. Three instruments, and each asks whether the target exists rather than whether it is the page the sentence meant.
obs The report card reading is the one I will remember. single-stranded graded A+/98 with truth_counted=100 (0 of 2 cited paths unresolved) while its first sentence was false -- and Truth is the GATED reading, the one that reads F below 60 whatever else scored. The instrument the tree trusts most to fail a false page is satisfied for free by the one link shape that cannot be wrong about anything else.
obs This is %430's shape in a second instrument on the same day. There a Register that measured nothing voted its ceiling; here a Truth that measured the wrong thing voted its ceiling. I did not go looking for that symmetry and would not have found it if the rota had not sent me to a different room.
obs The strongest evidence in the whole lap is a non-event: all three repaired pages grade EXACTLY as they did before -- A+/98, A/91, A+/98. The repair is invisible to the card, in both directions, which is the finding stated as a measurement rather than as an argument.
obs The repair declines to link what is gone. Both provenance lines name the elder in plain text and say which circled cut shed it, because linking a deleted path is a broken link and linking the living page is the fault itself. tools/fixtures/d/dated_path_exclusions.sh already carries both forwarding addresses, which is the tree having answered this question once already, in a room nobody thought to read from here.
obs A third instance turned up in the same room and is one line. foundations/README.md's Every Climate row carried the shed elder's stamp 20260821.035846 against the mutant it links -- the only one of 19 stamped rows whose stamp disagreed with its file. Fixing the stamp moved the row out of the table's newest-first order, so I moved the row too; a fix that trades one inconsistency for another is not a fix.
obs Measurement stopped a false booking as well. single-stranded is linked zero times in foundations/README.md, which looked like a second fault until I counted: 82 foundations against 19 rows. The table is a selection, not an index, and 63 pages are absent by design. I dropped it.
obs The guard is bounded to this tree's own provenance vocabulary rather than to self-links at large, and the bound is stated in its header rather than assumed: reimagining of, molt of, molted from, as the fossil, the elder. Run live it reads 5,455 documents, living 0, testimony 0.
obs The proof I care about is not the plants. Replayed against the two files exactly as they stood at HEAD, in a throwaway pen, the scan answers living_self_provenance=2 and names both files by line. A guard proven only against what its author invented has been tested by its author's imagination; this one is proven against the defect that actually happened.
obs The control proves 18 cases on real git repositories, every refusal from both sides -- planted, then removed and the reading returning green -- and the welcomes asserted as hard as the refusals, since seven honest sibling rosters on this pier depend on the distinction holding.
obs I rostered it at birth, tier lap. %360's whole lesson is that an unrostered guard is heard by nothing, and there is a mechanical edge besides: a new witness that nobody runs raises the unheard count by one against a ceiling of 1,116 that only falls, so an unrostered birth would have redded unheard_guard. It is GREEN with the row in place.
obs The pin went 678 bytes over bound with the row on it, and the law rather than a raise decides that: a finished section folds, and only a page whose LIVING parts outgrew its number earns a raise. All three standing rows read OPEN, so my own CLOSED row was the only finished section, and it folded to its own shelf minutes after it was written. The pin came back to 20,151.
obs I trimmed the row by about 1,100 bytes before folding it, which was the right order even though the fold made the bound moot -- an over-long row is over-long on a shelf too.
obs Fetch-before-book earned its place again. At the open --next read 432; when I fetched again before writing the row it read 435, three numbers spent by peers while I measured. The row is %435 and its stamp never moved. This is the fourth lap in a row where the number moved and the stamp did not, which is the standing argument for Keaton's open question about a claim on an OPEN row.
obs The cold pass read 113 guards, 106 green, 3 red, tree_moved=no. Two reds are known and gated -- agent_jail, and commit_message_guard, which is my own %431. The third is new: shell_dialect reds at gated_sed_i_sites=2 against a ceiling of 0, and both sites are lines 61 and 65 of tools/fixtures/f/fleet_key_locality_control.sh, the control pheromone landed thirty minutes earlier.
obs I left it alone on measurement rather than on manners. commit_message_guard withholds the roster receipt by itself, so repairing shell_dialect this lap would restore nothing, and the file belongs to the seat that wrote it and is thirty minutes old. The cure is already in the tree -- sed_inplace in tools/fixtures/s/shell_portable.sh -- so it is two lines for its author.
loom qa_report_card page=foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md before=A+/98 after=A+/98 truth_before=100 truth_after=100 note=repair_invisible_to_the_card
loom qa_report_card page=foundations/20260824-003828_every-climate-has-a-fiber.md before=A/91 after=A/91
loom qa_report_card page=foundations/README.md after=A+/98
loom self_link_census documents=5455 self_linking=35 living_foundations=9 provenance_lines=2 sibling_rosters=7 testimony=25
loom provenance_self_reference live_documents=5455 living=0 testimony=0 control_pass=18 control_fail=0 replay_at_head=2
loom roster pass=cold guards_run=113 guards_seconds=1217 green=106 red=3 gated=4 tree_moved=no reds=shell_dialect,agent_jail,commit_message_guard
loom reds_pin bytes_with_row=25254 bound=24576 rows_folded=1 bytes_after=20151 shelf=REDS-the-page-that-became-its-own-ancestor-rows-435.md
loom reds_spine next_at_open=432 next_at_book=435 peers_spent=3 row_stamp=20260905.160212
file foundations/20260823-204456_single-stranded.md the provenance line names the Radiant elder in plain text and the cut that shed it, rather than linking the reader's own page
file foundations/20260824-003828_every-climate-has-a-fiber.md the same repair, the same shape, the second of the two
file foundations/README.md the Every Climate row's stamp matched to the file it links, and the row moved to its sorted place
file tools/fixtures/p/provenance_self_reference_scan.sh the meter -- living self-provenance gated at zero, testimony reported, bounded to this tree's provenance vocabulary
file tools/fixtures/p/provenance_self_reference_control.sh 18 cases on real repositories, every refusal from both sides, the seven sibling rosters proven welcome
file tools/p/provenance_self_reference_witness.rish the witness, GREEN on metal and replayed against the defect as it stood at HEAD
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the guard rostered tier lap at birth, so it is heard rather than joining the 1,116 that are not
file construction/archive/REDS-the-page-that-became-its-own-ancestor-rows-435.md the row's shelf, folded the same lap it was written because the pin holds what is open
file construction/REDS.md %435 booked from the anointed spine after three peers spent 432 to 434, then folded to bring the pin back under bound
obs The rebase taught the lap one more thing, and it cost a renumber in the wrong direction. Upstream moved nine commits while I committed, and mid-conflict I ran reds_spine_derive_scan.sh --next and read 436, so I renumbered the row, the shelf filename, the recital, the card and this log from %435 to %436.
obs It was wrong. The anointed spine's highest row is %434 -- xy/main at e831f252c carries no %435 at all -- and --next answered 436 because the tree it read was mid-rebase and already held my own unshared row at 435. reds_ledger_monotone caught it immediately: expected row 435, found 436, gaps_or_dupes=1. I put every one of the six sites back to %435 and the spine reads 1..435 whole.
obs That is %428's lesson in the ledger's own instrument rather than in the round-open: every later step misreads a standing rebase. The round-open now clears an interrupted rebase before anything reads the tree, and I read a number off a tree that was standing in one. The habit the card already carries -- take the number from --next, never from the one written in the row -- needs one more clause: and never from a tree mid-rebase.
obs The rebase also carried the card 397 bytes over its ceiling, since upstream's live front landed on top of mine. Three condensations closed it and all three were landed accounts rather than open rows -- my own paragraph tightened twice, the %423-%426 line reduced to its shelf pointer after checking all three of its examples stand there, and the LIVE FRONT NOW FOLDS announcement reduced to the policy it seated. The cairn names what left and says which sentence is worth recalling.
loom reds_spine anointed_max=434 next_clean=435 next_mid_rebase=436 renumbered=6_sites cause=read_during_conflicted_rebase corrected=435
loom itinerary bytes_after_rebase=33165 bound=32768 condensations=3 bytes_final=32668
recommend keep-going -- the lane's own queue is still gated on Keaton (%430 edits a seated assertion, %431 touches gate %1), yet the rota keeps finding work in the rooms it sends me to, and the next Air lap has a fence post already named: shell_dialect's two sed -i sites belong to pheromone and the cure is written.
